  "mechanisms": [
    "Urban sounds increase BOLD signal complexity (BEN) due to uncertainty and chaotic information processing, potentially leading to negative affect.",
    "Nature sounds increase functional connectivity (FC) in auditory, cinguloopercular, and somatomotor networks, which is associated with improved cognitive performance, suggesting enhanced brain processing efficiency.",
    "Lower FC in urban sound conditions may reflect less efficient processing or increased distraction, potentially linking to cognitive decline and mental health risks (e.g., schizophrenia)."
  ],
  "moderators": [],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "The findings suggest that exposure to natural soundscapes can have beneficial effects on brain function and cognitive performance, while urban soundscapes may have negative consequences for affect and brain complexity. This supports the importance of incorporating natural sound elements into urban design or providing access to natural environments."
  ],
  "domains": [
    "A5_Acoustic",
